      en: "Taung Kwe Pagoda sits on a hill in Shan State, about 20 kilometers from Taunggyi. It consists of a stupa and several shrines, offering stunning views of Inle Lake and surrounding mountains. The pagoda is an important Buddhist pilgrimage site. Legend says it was built by King Alaungsithu in the 12th century. A notable feature is a large Buddha statue seated on a lotus throne. The complex is surrounded by trees, and a covered path leads to the summit.",
